+				nid = NUMA_NO_NODE;
+
+			new_hub = kzalloc_node(bytes, GFP_KERNEL, nid);
+		}
Reason:
The fix introduces an explicit check: when `uv_blade_to_node(bid)` equals `SOCK_EMPTY`, the node ID is replaced with `NUMA_NO_NODE`. `NUMA_NO_NODE` is a safe fallback that tells `kzalloc_node` to allocate memory on any valid node, avoiding the panic caused by the invalid 0xffff value. This ensures that deconfigured sockets still receive their hub info structures without crashing the system.

